       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe maximum for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This dose carries a significant risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nSome options, depending on what you intended:\n1. **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3000 mg/day). This is a common standard dose.\n2. **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4000 mg/day). This is the maximum, and you'd typically use it only if there are no risk factors.\n3. **650 mg by mouth four times daily** (2600 mg/day).\n\nIf the 2000 mg dose was intentional, for example because of a specific protocol, tell me and I'll reconsider. Otherwise, tell me which of these you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
