       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I understand you've confirmed it, but 6000 mg/day of acetaminophen is 50% above the labeled maximum. Taken repeatedly, that dose can cause serious liver injury, and I don't know of a standard protocol that supports it for an adult inpatient. Your confirmation didn't include a clinical rationale, and I can't judge whether one exists.\n\nHere are some ways to get the order placed:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit.** I can place 1000 mg PO three or four times daily (3000 or 4000 mg/day) right now.\n- **Add more analgesia.** If pain control is the concern, I can enter a non-acetaminophen option alongside it. Tell me which drug and dose you want.\n- **Go through pharmacy.** If you have a specific reason for the higher dose, you can enter it directly in the order system. A pharmacist or attending can then review it and override the hard stop.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the in-range options?"
